Description:
    Emits the admin pages for one model: a controller, a Phlex index and show
    view, a request spec, and a route.

    The pages are plain Phlex classes you own and edit afterwards. What keeps
    them looking alike as models are added is the Views::Admin kit they render
    (Heading, Table, FieldList, Field, Json) — not this generator, which never
    runs over the same model twice.

    Fields are guessed from the table's columns, which is a starting point, not
    an answer: the labels and the blurb are written for a reader, and the
    generator only knows column names.

Example:
    bin/rails generate admin:resource ApiCall

    Creates:
        app/controllers/settings/api_calls_controller.rb
        app/views/settings/api_calls/index.rb
        app/views/settings/api_calls/show.rb
        spec/requests/settings/api_calls_spec.rb
    And adds to config/routes.rb, inside `namespace :settings`:
        resources :api_calls, only: [:index, :show]

    The pages hang off the Admin page at /settings/admin: that is where their
    breadcrumbs lead back through, and where you add the card linking to them.
    The trail is written into the templates rather than derived from --namespace,
    so a page emitted elsewhere needs its own.

        The index pages by cursor, newest first (Admin::Page). A list people read by
        name rather than by date passes its own ordering, which wants a matching
        compound index. Filters are per-resource and hand-added — see
        ApiCalls::Listing for the shape.

Options:
    --columns=created_at service_name kind   Index table columns, in order.
    --namespace=settings                     Controller/view/route namespace.
    --destroy                                Add a destroy action and a Remove button.
